--
N5008 [class.base.init]/2: a mem-initializer-id may name a base class
through a typedef-name; here the virtual base ios<C> of the class template
ostream<C> is named through the member typedef ios_type.  The front end
reports "symbol 'ios_type' is unknown" and drops the constructor.  This is
libstdc++'s basic_ostream / basic_istream move constructors
(`: __ios_type()', ostream:440, istream:576/703), dropped in
cpp11_ofstream_from_string and the goto-programs TUs; test_libstdcxx.desc
is that program and forbids only the ostream:440 drop.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept both programs.  Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
